{"text": "Apple’s latest filed risk language points first to tariffs and other trade measures, which it says can materially hurt operations, supply chain, pricing and gross margin [f_3956f8e19f14]. It also flags trade and other international disputes as a risk because they can weaken consumer spending and sentiment for its products and services [f_3956f8e19f14]. More broadly, it says macroeconomic conditions, including inflation, interest rates and currency fluctuations, can materially affect results [f_3956f8e19f14], and it also highlights risks around new business strategies, acquisitions, legal and regulatory compliance, and litigation or government investigations [f_a7676712d462].

